📅 Day 5 – Looping Statements

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on looping statements, which are used to execute a block of code repeatedly based on a condition.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ for Loop

Used when the number of iterations is known. It consists of initialization, condition, and increment/decrement.

2️⃣ while Loop

An entry-controlled loop that executes as long as the condition is true.

3️⃣ do-while Loop

An exit-controlled loop that executes the code block at least once before checking the condition.

🔹 Key Concepts Learned

Difference between entry-controlled and exit-controlled loops.

Importance of loop control variables.

How improper conditions can lead to infinite loops.

Practical understanding of how loops reduce code repetition.

🎯 Learning Outcome

Understood how repetition works in Java programs.

Learned differences between for, while, and do-while.

Strengthened logical thinking and program flow understanding.